# Edge compromise direction

Product mandate ([`docs/mandate.md`](../../docs/mandate.md)): build a **good
inference engine at any scale**. That trajectory does not change.

**When a design must compromise**, prefer **edge / embedded performance**
(tight RAM/CPU, WASM, Raspberry Pi–class ARM) over datacenter-only assumptions.

When adding features, loaders, backends, or acceptance:

- Keep one engine story across scales — do not fork a “cloud engine.”
- If you must choose (API shape, default budgets, what CI gates, what to defer),
  choose the option that stays viable on edge/embedded hosts.
- Park datacenter-only techniques in [`docs/inspiration/`](../../docs/inspiration/)
  until a user story claims them.
